# PLCAutoPilot Core

AI-powered PLC programming platform: Next.js web app + Python automation for Schneider, Siemens, Rockwell, Mitsubishi, and CODESYS.

## Repo layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/` | Next.js 15 routes, API handlers (`app/api/ai-*`, `generate-plc`), feature pages |
| `lib/` | Claude SDK (`claude.ts`), Drizzle DB, PLC model DB, simulation/digital twin |
| `automation/` | Python PLC automation — run scripts from here (`cd automation`) |
| `automation/plc_automation/` | Fast API + PLCopen XML (`PLCAutomation`, `Platform`) |
| `automation/plc_file_handler/` | Parse/generate vendor project files (`cli.py`) |
| `docs/` | Categorized documentation — index at `docs/README.md` |
| `.claude/skills/` | Full platform reference docs (XML schemas, patterns, activation rules) |
| `.cursor/skills/` | Cursor agent workflows that point to `.claude/skills/` |

## Commands

- Web: `npm install && npm run dev` (needs `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, Postgres via Docker)
- DB: `docker compose up -d && npm run db:migrate`
- Python tests: `python automation/plc_automation/tests.py`
- Runbook: `docs/RUNBOOK.md`

## Agent conventions

- Follow root `CLAUDE.md` (Karpathy guidelines): think first, minimal scope, surgical diffs.
- Keep new docs under `docs/`; use the `organize-docs` skill when stray `.md` files appear.
- Load platform skills before generating PLC programs (see `.cursor/skills/`).
- No emojis in project code or UI; use Google Material Icons.
- Do not commit unless the user asks. Do not push unless the user asks.

## Safety (mandatory)

PLCAutoPilot drafts code only. All generated ladder logic must be reviewed, tested, and validated by certified engineers before production deployment (IEC 61131-3 / IEC 61508).
